         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Introduction\n\nIn **First Steps (Counting)**, we saw that in Mesoamerica the Indigenous peoples used their own bodies — especially their hands — to create a numerical system that was used for more than a thousand years.\n\nBut that is not the only remarkable feature of these numbers. In this class, we will discover more about them.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "5b8aceeb-416e-4ce4-9a5d-90bc05c52aa7",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "5b8aceeb-416e-4ce4-9a5d-90bc05c52aa7",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "inlove",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "87b260d5-4992-4ec2-8ba2-96a8dfa16c89",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=87b260d5-4992-4ec2-8ba2-96a8dfa16c89",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### The Numerical System\n\nThe peoples who lived in Mesoamerica created symbols to count, mainly to record time, as we can see on the stelae that have been discovered.\n\nOne important characteristic of these symbols is that they are **not decimal** like the Hindu-Arabic numbers we use today: they are **vigesimal**, which means they have 20 different numbers representing values between 0 and 19.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "106f8c27-b834-4f16-be29-57f5a0e58fcf",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "106f8c27-b834-4f16-be29-57f5a0e58fcf",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "shocking",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "87b260d5-4992-4ec2-8ba2-96a8dfa16c89",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=87b260d5-4992-4ec2-8ba2-96a8dfa16c89",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### 19 or 3 Symbols?\n\nTo build the numbers they used for counting, they combined just **three different symbols** to produce the first 20 numbers: zero, one and five.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p data-custom=\"maya-symbols-0-1-5\"></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "b8d4fb5b-ce64-42cb-b8e9-aceba1312aa4",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "b8d4fb5b-ce64-42cb-b8e9-aceba1312aa4",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "thinking",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "87b260d5-4992-4ec2-8ba2-96a8dfa16c89",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=87b260d5-4992-4ec2-8ba2-96a8dfa16c89",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Did They Discover the Zero?\n\nAs we explained in another class in **First Steps (Counting)** — *We Have Zero* — there are different concepts of zero. There is no doubt that the Maya had a symbol for zero; however, until today we have not been able to find a use of zero like the one in our current numerical systems.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "93df3ab3-5e2c-4546-8e1d-c15905ab0738",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "93df3ab3-5e2c-4546-8e1d-c15905ab0738",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "happy",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "87b260d5-4992-4ec2-8ba2-96a8dfa16c89",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=87b260d5-4992-4ec2-8ba2-96a8dfa16c89",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### How to Write Numbers?\n\nWhen we write the numbers from 0 to 5, we always use one symbol per line:",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p data-custom=\"maya-table-0-5\"></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "f358fdc7-8239-4795-a1ce-4d8090dee40e",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": null,
         "score": 1,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "f358fdc7-8239-4795-a1ce-4d8090dee40e",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "thinking",
         "source_menu": [],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Thinking\n\nFor values between 0 and 5, we use only one line — the same values we can represent with one hand.\n\nTo write numbers between 6 and 10, will we put other values to the left?",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
         "next": "f2c8655a-9342-41e3-bcf9-77155b884bef",
         "prev": "",
         "jumpTo": "",
         "answer": "no",
         "score": 2,
         "position": ""
      },
      {
         "id": "f2c8655a-9342-41e3-bcf9-77155b884bef",
         "audio": "",
         "smile": "happy",
         "source_menu": [
            {
               "type": 1,
               "uuid": "87b260d5-4992-4ec2-8ba2-96a8dfa16c89",
               "text": "Original Text",
               "page": "https://www.historytracers.org/index.html?page=class_content&arg=87b260d5-4992-4ec2-8ba2-96a8dfa16c89",
               "date_time": {
                  "type": "gregory",
                  "year": "2026",
                  "month": "",
                  "day": ""
               }
            }
         ],
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Vertical, Not Horizontal\n\nTo make Mesoamerican numbers grow, we write values on another line, and not to the left. Below, we write the numbers from 6 to 10.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p data-custom=\"maya-table-6-10\"></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ],
         "desc": null,
